  <section class="faq-section">
    <div class="narrow">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Questions?</p>
        <h2 class="section-h2">Everything <em>you might be wondering.</em></h2>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <details>
          <summary>How quickly do updates sync to the portals?</summary>
          <p>Most portals pull the XML feed every 15-60 minutes, so changes typically appear within an hour. Some portals sync faster. The feed itself updates within seconds of you saving a change in PropertyList - the delay is on the portal's end, not ours.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <details>
          <summary>Can I send to multiple portals with one feed?</summary>
          <p>Yes. Your XML feed URL is the same for every portal - you just give the same URL to each portal's data team. One update in PropertyList, one feed, every portal picks it up automatically. No separate feeds per portal.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <details>
          <summary>Do the portals need to accept XML? What if mine don't?</summary>
          <p>All major Spanish and international property portals accept XML feeds - it's the industry standard for bulk property data. If you're not sure whether a specific portal you use accepts feeds, <a href="https://wa.me/34610951177">WhatsApp us</a> and we'll check for you. We include setup support with every export subscription.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <details>
          <summary>What does the XML feed include? Photos, descriptions, all of it?</summary>
          <p>Yes - the feed includes everything: photos, full descriptions, prices, floor areas, bedrooms, bathrooms, location data, property type, status (available / under offer / sold), and any custom fields you've filled in. Whatever's in your PropertyList property record goes into the feed.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <details>
          <summary>What's the difference between import and export?</summary>
          <p><strong>Import</strong> brings listings into PropertyList from an external source - for example, if you work with another agency's feed or have listings on another CRM you want to consolidate. This is free forever. <strong>Export</strong> pushes your PropertyList listings outward to your website, Idealista, Kyero, Rightmove and any other portal. This is the paid feature (from 35€/month).</p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <details>
          <summary>I already have a website. How do I connect it?</summary>
          <p>Your website just needs to accept an XML feed URL - most property website platforms do this natively. Once you activate export in your settings, you get a feed URL to paste into your CMS. If you need help, our setup support is included and we can walk you through it. <a href="https://wa.me/34610951177">WhatsApp us &rarr;</a></p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <details>
          <summary>I don't have a website. Can I still use the export?</summary>
          <p>Yes - you can push to external portals (Idealista, Kyero, Rightmove etc.) without having your own website. If you'd like a website too, the <a href="https://info.propertylist.es/website-builder">PropertyList Website Builder</a> gives you a fully branded site with your listings auto-loaded from 50€/month - build and preview free.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <details>
          <summary>What happens to my portal listings if I cancel?</summary>
          <p>Your portals keep whatever they last pulled from your feed. The listings don't disappear immediately, but they'll stop updating - so portals may eventually mark them as inactive or remove them. Your PropertyList CRM data is yours and stays intact regardless.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

